WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.934
-Good evening.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.033
I'm Seth Meyers,
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.200
We hope you're
all doing well tonight.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.567
Now let's get to the news.

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:09.467
Democrat Eric Adams defeated
Republican Curtis Sliwa

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.934
yesterday in New York City's
mayoral election.

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:15.100
Adams will take office
on January 1st,

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.167
which means, on January 2nd,

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:20.167
cab drivers will start
blaming him for traffic.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:21.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.400
"You believe this?
Freakin' Adams."

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:26.434
President Biden
returned early this morning

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:28.501
to Washington
from his trip to Europe.

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:32.033
And now he won't stop calling
the White House his flat.

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.467
Yesterday's New Jersey
gubernatorial race

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:39.267
between Democratic governor
Phil Murphy

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:42.300
and Republican Jack Ciatterelli
remains too close to call.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.300
In fact, as of our taping time,

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.367
both candidates were yelling,
"You take it!

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:49.834
No, you take it!"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:53.033
House speaker Nancy Pelosi
told reporters yesterday

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:55.634
that while she did not announce
a vote for President Biden's

00:00:55.634 --> 00:01:00.701
$1.75 trillion economic agenda,
she believes disputes around it

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:02.767
could be resolved
by the end of the day.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:05.400
Okay, it could.
But will it?

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.100
I feel like we've been waiting
around for this budget bill

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.400
for longer than we've been
waiting for "Avatar 2."

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:15.400
Build Back Better is basically
Biden's unobtainium.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.434
[ Laughter ]
And if you don't get that joke,

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:20.300
it's because we've be waiting
forever for "Avatar 2."

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:26.400
Unobtainium jokes used to land.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.467
Senate Majority Leader
Chuck Schumer said yesterday

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:30.400
that lawmakers
have reached a deal

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.000
to lower prescription-drug
prices for seniors.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.767
So, now they just need
to draft it up, print it out,

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:37.767
and send it to Joe's desk
for approval.

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.033
Nope, wrong Joe.
Oh, there we go.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.634
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:45.067
New York mayor --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:50.033
[ Loud groan ]

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:51.601
New York mayor Bill de Blasio

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:53.968
suggested in an interview
yesterday that he is running

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:57.267
for governor after years
of running from governor.

00:01:57.267 --> 00:01:59.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:01.334
McDonald's, this year,
is celebrating

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:03.868
the 40th anniversary
of its McRib sandwich.

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:07.133
But, if anyone asks,
it was made today.

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:10.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:13.000
Reality star Kendall Jenner
turned 26 today

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.901
even though her mom specifically
asked her not to.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:18.801
"25 plays better."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.634
A new study suggests
that married couples

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:22.000
who met on dating apps

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.667
have a higher chance
of getting a divorce.

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:25.801
"Well, that was kind of
the point," said a couple

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:29.534
who met on "Divorcr."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:33.200
97-year-old Vito Perillo
was re-elected mayor yesterday

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.734
of a town in New Jersey
because he, once again,

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:38.100
failed to break
the witch's curse.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:42.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:45.000
After the --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.767
After the
"Pirates of the Caribbean" ride

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:48.601
at Disneyland malfunctioned
on Sunday,

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.734
guests had to wait 90 minutes
until employees

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.801
were able to push their boats
to the exit.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:55.067
"We were sitting there
for what felt like hours,

00:02:55.067 --> 00:02:58.400
and nothing was happening,"
said someone watching the movie.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:02.067
-Ooh!

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:03.300
Dunkin' --
[ Laughs ]

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.834
A very -- a very late zing.

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:07.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:09.767
"Pirates of the --"
[ Laughing ]

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:10.934
Those filmmakers were like,

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.133
"I think
we're out of the woods."

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:16.834
"Been over a decade."

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:18.434
"Well, at least they're not
going after 'Avatar.'

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:22.167
They are?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:24.234
Dunkin' Donuts announced
new flavors this week

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:25.567
for their holiday lineup,

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:28.133
including a toasted
white-chocolate signature latte

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.067
and white mocha hot chocolate.

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:31.901
And if you want to see
what those drinks look like,

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:34.868
check out Ben Affleck's
paparazzi photos next week.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:37.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:40.667
Finally, the animal rights group
PETA last week called on

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:43.400
Major League Baseball
to stop using the term bullpen

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.267
for the area
where pitchers warm up

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:46.667
because it references the place

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.200
where cattle
are kept before slaughter.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.100
Instead, they suggested
using the more

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.133
animal-friendly term "arm barn."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:55.334
That one got the most attention,
but there are several other

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.667
animal-themed terms PETA
would like to see changed.

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.400
For example --
We're gonna do some now.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.467
For example --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:02.801
That's what
this whole bit's gonna be.

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:05.300
For example --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.734
The --
[ Laughs ]

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:08.767
The supermarket chain
Piggly Wiggly

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:10.868
is offensive to pigs,
as pigs do not have hips

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:12.434
that are conducive to wiggling,
so...

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:13.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.334
...they suggested
changing the store's name

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:16.567
to Broccoli Woccoli.

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:18.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:19.934
Having ants in your pants
would be

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:21.767
an uncomfortable sensation
for a human.

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.634
But just imagine how cruel --

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:25.534
how cruel an experience
for the ant.

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:26.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:28.968
Especially in a corduroy
or rigid denim.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:32.000
So, next time you're
feeling anxious or restless,

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.067
may we suggest the term
"beans in your jeans"?

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:36.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:38.100
If you're at a party,
and it's all dudes,

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.634
rather than
triggering vegetarians

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:41.200
and people suffering
from hypertension

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.701
by calling it a "sausage fest,"
they suggest a call it

00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:47.334
something less offensive,
like a "Boner-roo Teste-val."

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:51.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:54.400
And they appreciate that's --
that's a mouthful.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:58.033
Moving on,
nature's greatest pollinators

00:04:58.033 --> 00:05:00.801
have six sections to their legs
and don't appreciate you

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:03.367
patella-fetishists
focusing on just the one,

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:06.033
so stop calling something neat
the "bee's knees"

00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:08.167
and instead say
it's the yam's gams.

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:10.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:12.100
And I know that's hard
for all of you

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.167
who are still saying
the bee's knees.

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:16.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:18.467
Up next, instead of saying
"like a fish out of water"

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:20.067
and invoking
the horror of suffocation

00:05:20.067 --> 00:05:22.901
to our scaly cousins,
say "like a vaccinated person

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:25.033
in the fire department."
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:30.033
And...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:32.567
Instead of saying "Larry Bird,"
which could cause a sparrow

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:35.200
to turn and say "What?"
before plowing into a window,

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:38.667
say "Danny Ainge."
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:40.567
Keep that one for the "best of."

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:46.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:49.567
Next up --
[ Laughs ]

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:51.501
We're only -- Wait.
We're only a tenth of the way

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:53.434
through this?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:55.701
Next, instead of saying,
"He sleeps with the fishes,"

00:05:55.701 --> 00:05:58.133
which is straight-up
slut shaming, he said --

00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:00.868
say, "He caught COVID
from an unvaccinated fireman."

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:04.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.234
And instead of saying,
"He's no spring chicken,"

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:09.667
needlessly reminding the birds
of their inescapable mortality,

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:11.968
say, "He looking like
an heirloom gourd."

00:06:11.968 --> 00:06:13.300
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.334
Moving on --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:17.067
Moving on, instead of saying
"There's plenty of fish

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:18.901
in the sea," which ignores
the devastating effects

00:06:18.901 --> 00:06:21.067
of commercial overfishing,
say, "Look, Linda,

00:06:21.067 --> 00:06:22.734
you had to have known
this was a real possibility

00:06:22.734 --> 00:06:24.701
when your fireman boyfriend
decided not to get vaccinated."

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.734
[ Laughter ]
And, finally, when it's time

00:06:26.734 --> 00:06:28.734
for the talk, rather than
teaching your children

00:06:28.734 --> 00:06:31.000
about the birds and bees,
whose sex lives

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.367
are nobody's damn business
but their own,

00:06:33.367 --> 00:06:34.901
teach them about the zucchini
and the pumpkin

00:06:34.901 --> 00:06:36.067
with a hole carved into it.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.067 --> 00:06:38.968
This has been other
animal-themed terms.

00:06:38.968 --> 00:06:41.467
I told you it was a bit.
PETA would like to see change.

